# Server-only secrets and sensitive logic

This is a **Next.js App Router** project (`src/app/`). Sensitive work must stay on the server.

## Required boundaries

| Concern | Allowed locations | Never in |
|---------|-------------------|----------|
| Stripe secret keys (`STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, webhooks) | `src/app/api/**/route.ts`, `src/lib/server/**` | Client components, `public/`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` |
| Odoo API keys, JWT private keys, SMTP creds | `src/lib/server/**` + API routes | Client bundle |
| File/DB persistence (`.data/`, `fs`, portal stores) | `src/lib/server/**` + API routes | `"use client"` files |
| OTP issue/verify (`issueOtp`, `verifyOtp`, `getTestOtpCode`) | `src/lib/server/**` + `/api/auth/forgot-password/*` | Client components |

## Client components (`"use client"`)

- Call **`/api/*` routes** for auth, payments, orders, subscriptions.
- Import **types only** from `src/types/*` — never `@/lib/server/*` (except type-only paths that must live in shared types).
- Use `src/lib/access-token.ts` for in-memory JWT storage; refresh via httpOnly cookie.

## Environment variables

- **No secrets** with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix.
- Server secrets: `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `ODOO_API_KEY`, `JWT_PRIVATE_KEY`, `SMTP_PASS`, `PII_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, `OTP_TEST_CODE`.
- Public URLs use server env `PORTAL_BASE_URL` in email templates — not `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.

## Enforcement

Runs automatically on every commit via Husky (`npm run prepare`).

```bash
npm run check:boundary
```

This fails if `lib/server` imports, `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, or secret env refs appear outside `app/api/` and `lib/server/`.

Production requires `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL` + `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN` for OTP and rate limits. `isDemoMode()` and `isTestOtpEnabled()` hard-return `false` when `NODE_ENV === "production"`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — client component
"use client";
import { getStripeConfig } from "@/lib/server/config";

// ✅ GOOD — API route
import { createStripePaymentIntent } from "@/lib/server/stripe";
export async function POST(request: NextRequest) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — client calls API
await authFetch("/api/payments/checkout", { method: "POST", body: ... });
```
